{"base_rate":0.3085271317829457,"brier":0.16461689922480618,"bss":0.2283756732090949,"bss_hi":0.3227962932215896,"bss_lo":0.10949437672524297,"chart":{"base":[462.1,170.1],"fp":[275.3,215.0],"lead":"62,168.7 272,134.2 482,101.4 692,9.8","note":{"base":"skill 0.23 — higher than 23% of cities","fp":"low end +7pp, high end +22pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.9 °C — better than 6% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 5%; promised 93% → rained 69%"},"rel":"65.2,443.8 113.9,380.9 315.4,231.9 647.4,168"},"country":"US","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.11784496124031008,"ess":501.7878714665374,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Chicago</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Chicago rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 7 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>71%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>3%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 645 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nCHICAGO 3.6 NNW, 8.9 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.23, ranked 103 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(65&ndash;118) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>3%</b></td><td class='num'>159</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>1%</td><td class='num'><b>9%</b></td><td class='num'>94</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>11%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'><b>28%</b></td><td class='num'>68</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>26%</td><td class='num'><b>47%</b></td><td class='num'>66</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>54%</td><td class='num'><b>62%</b></td><td class='num'>65</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>86%</td><td class='num'><b>67%</b></td><td class='num'>64</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>71%</b></td><td class='num'>65</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">7 of 8 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Chicago</b> <span class=\"muted\">US</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">7 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.23</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>65&ndash;118\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>645 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Chicago &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Chicago\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"char